warmup and controlled learning rate annealing. This stabilizes training and prevents large early updates that contribute to overfitting. Historical experiments show OneCycleLR with warmup improves convergence and generalization. Keep other training hyperparameters unchanged (batch size, weight decay, label smoothing, gradient clipping). Implementation: import torch.optim.lr_scheduler.OneCycleLR, set scheduler = OneCycleLR(optimizer, max_lr=LEARNING_RATE, steps_per_epoch=len(train_loader), epochs=NUM_EPOCHS, pct_start=0.1, div_factor=25, final_div_factor=1e4), and replace scheduler.step() call after each batch (not epoch) since OneCycleLR updates per step."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
