dropout 0.1. Add an SWA callback that, starting from epoch 3 (after warmup), maintains an averaged copy of model weights after each epoch. The final model used for inference is the averaged weights. Additionally, implement layer-wise learning rate decay (LLRD) by setting the classifier head's learning rate to 2e-5 and backbone layers to 2e-6. Use AdamW optimizer. This directly addresses overfitting and underfitting seen in the initial plan.", "training_evaluation": "Replace the linear warmup scheduler with cosine annealing schedule (T_max=40) with warmup restarts for 10% of steps. Train for 40 epochs with early stopping patience of 5 on SWA validation loss (compute loss using averaged model). Use class-balanced (CB) loss with beta=0.999 to re-weight samples inversely to effective number per class. Modify Compute_log_loss to handle row normalization as in evaluation. Save the SWA model checkpoint. This matches historical successful experiments that used cosine annealing and class weights to improve generalization."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
