    "model_design": "Replace the default CLS token pooling in AutoModelForSequenceClassification with a learned attention-weighted mean pooling layer on top of the encoder's last hidden states. Add a custom classification head that takes the weighted average of all 512 hidden states (or the pooled output from attention) and maps to 3 classes. The attention weights are computed as Softmax(ReLU(hidden_states @ W_attn)). This modification addresses the root cause of discarding distributed stylistic markers, following successful historical patterns of using attention pooling."
  }
